WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.700
Good morning Hank, it's Monday, November 5th. Today's video comes in ten parts.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.680
Ten parts! Are you crazy?!

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.940
I know it's madness. But the good news is each part is going to be extremely short. Like what we just did...

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.940
What you mean this back and forth?

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.940
Yeah exactly. That was part one.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.960
Wow! You didn't even introduce the part. You just BAM went right into it.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.400
I know. We could just keep talking about what a great trick it was but I gotta move onto part two.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.460
Part two: Hank, thanks to you and Dad for that video you dug up of me at the Orange County Public School Author Awards.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.080
It was quite interesting for me to see the way I responded to the compliment my writing ever received from a peer.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:49.340
And while I'm tempted to agree with you that that moment represented the first time I realized that my writing could connect me to other people and to the world,

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:54.840
I think it's far more likely that that was the first moment I ever realized that a girl might, for even one second, like me.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.100
Part three: Pakistan. Listen up General Musharraf, 'cause I know you watch this show.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.580
You're pissing me off. Stop it!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:06.200
Part four: Paper Towns. Hank the ball that is Paper Towns is back in the court that is  my house

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:13.240
which means that for the next week or so I'm going to be editing like 14 hours a day, and its going to be very stressful.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.800
So anyway Hank, I feel like I should tell you that this week's video blogs are going to be kind like

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.980
Alberto Contador at the Tour de France, which is to say that I'm going to go really fast and I might have to use steroids to do it.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:27.180
Part five: Ear worms. Hank you know how sometimes a tune or a lyric from a song will get stuck in your head, like... you know like...

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:34.420
"I need Harry Potter like a Grindylow needs water, and as Saturday approaches my need grows!"

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.840
Like that. Well lately I've been having poetry ear worms. Like this from Walt Whitman:

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:46.400
"Has anyone supposed it is lucky to be born? Well I hasten to tell him or her, that it is just as lucky to die, and I know it."

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:53.000
Part six: Nerdfighter Like. Hank I have great news we've raised enough money through the generosity of many many Nerdfighters

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.560
that now we can bring our secret sibling and her and her secret Nerdfighter boy together so that their awesome can collide

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.700
And cause an awesome mushroom cloud that will spread awesome fallout all throughout the world.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.760
Hank even though they have basically been outed in My Pants, I'm still not going to say their names until they say that it is okay.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:15.160
But I have to tell you they are so cute! Hank they are so cute they could beat any of the puppies or kittens on 'Cute with Chris'.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:22.680
Part seven: Pakistan again. I mean seriously George Bush, have you ever liked a leader of a country that turned out not to be a total jackass?!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.440
Like, remember when you first met with Vladimir Putin and you said you could see into his soul and you saw that it was a good soul?

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.800
Excellent call, George Bush.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.600
And then do you remember all of the wonderful things you said about Musharraf?

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.240
It's almost like you have really questionable judgement.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.920
Part eight: One more thing about Pakistan. Hank, I don't know if you can tell that I am really mad about what's happening in Pakistan right now.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:46.400
Do you remember in 2003 and 2004 and 2005 when President Bush would say over and over again:

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.540
"Democracy is on the march"

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.000
Um... Where is it marching to?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Because it is not marching to Pakistan,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.560
and it's not marching to Russia,

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.460
it's not marching to Nepal, it's not marching to China,

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.460
it's not marching to Saudi Arabia,

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.020
it's not marching to Libya, or Kuwait, or Oman, or Qatar,

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.400
it's not marching to Venezuela.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:09.740
In fact if you do a count, you might find out that there are fewer genuinely democratic countries today then there were when democracy started marching.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.240
Hank, maybe democracy is marching to Mars.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.180
Which I'm sure is great for the Martians, but it's a disaster for us.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.220
Hank, we have got to get democracy off the march immediately!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.600
Part nine: the outro. Hank, it looks like the people of Pakistan are going to be less free tomorrow than they are today.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.880
Just as they are less free today than they were yesterday. I don't look forward to seeing that tomorrow.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.880
But I do look forward to seeing you.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.980
Part ten: the scavenger hunt. Hank, Nerdfighters have found clues all over the United States.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:43.380
They found a dollar bill in Indianapolis, a dollar bill in Englewood, Florida, and a note just outside of Chicago.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:46.080
They have de-anagramed all the anagrams in the notes.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.080
And they have found the video we have hid for them.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.300
Now we are going to calm down for a day and just chat.

